# Exploratory Data Analysis on Retail Sales Data

**Intern: [Adams Salamatu]
**Track: Data Analytics
**Task:** Level 1, Task 1: EDA on Retail Sales Data
**Internship: Oasis Infobyte (OIBSIP)

## Project Overview
An exploratory data analysis of a retail sales dataset (1,000 transactions from 2023) to uncover sales trends, customer behaviour and actionable business insights.

## Dataset
Retail Sales Dataset from Kaggle: [https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/mohammadtalib786/retail-sales-dataset]

## Tools Used
Python, pandas, matplotlib, seaborn, Jupyter Notebook

## What the Notebook Covers
- Data loading and initial inspection (shape, data types, null check)
- Descriptive statistics (mean, median, mode, standard deviation)
- Time series analysis (monthly and quarterly sales trends)
- Customer demographics (age groups and gender)
- Product category analysis (units sold and revenue)
- Correlation heatmap
- Additional analysis: revenue by age group and product category
- Conclusion with business recommendations

## Key Findings
- Sales were volatile: May was the strongest month and September the weakest, with Q4 the strongest quarter and Q3 the weakest.
- Electronics earned the most revenue, while Clothing sold the most units.
- Price per Unit has the strongest link to revenue (correlation 0.85), while age has almost no link to total spending.
- Age does affect what customers buy: for example, Clothing sells best to 26-35year-olds.
